DESIGN
- Four path-filtered workflows authored, one per platform, per the spec table:
    apps-shared.yml   paths: apps/shared/**, api/openapi/**            runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    apps-windows.yml  paths: apps/windows/**, apps/shared/**, api/openapi/**  runs-on: windows-latest
    apps-android.yml  paths: apps/android/**, apps/shared/**, api/openapi/**  runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    apps-apple.yml    paths: apps/apple/**, apps/shared/**, api/openapi/**    runs-on: macos-latest
  Each workflow also self-triggers on changes to its own file.
- Triggers: pull_request (paths only) + push to the ADR-007 program branch
  (feat/apps-shared|windows|android|apple, paths-filtered) + workflow_dispatch.
- Concurrency: group per ref (apps-<platform>-${{ github.ref }}); cancel-in-progress
  only on pull_request so push/main runs complete.
- Caches: setup-java cache:gradle (shared+android); actions/cache NuGet (windows);
  actions/cache SPM/.build + DerivedData SourcePackages (apple).
- ADR-010 triad per platform, each step surfaces non-zero exit, NO continue-on-error:
    shared : gradlew :shared:build | ktlintCheck+detekt | gradlew :shared:test
    windows: dotnet build -c Release | dotnet format --verify-no-changes | dotnet test
    android: gradlew assembleDebug | ktlintCheck+detekt+lint | gradlew test
    apple  : xcodebuild build | swiftlint --strict + swiftformat --lint | xcodebuild test
- NO-OP-BUT-VALID guard (not a bare exit 0): a "Detect buildable project (guard)"
  step inspects the program dir for a real build target
  (gradlew/build.gradle.kts/settings.gradle.kts; .sln/.csproj; Package.swift/.xcodeproj).
    * none present  -> sets buildable=false, prints documented GUARD lines, passes.
    * present       -> sets buildable=true; build/lint/test steps run via
                       `if: steps.detect.outputs.buildable == 'true'` and FAIL if the
                       project exists but does not build/lint/test.
- Final "CI honesty marker" step echoes EXIT=0 only on `if: success()`.

